  "note": "Seven Nationalist candidates for six seats, after five of twelve nominees withdrew (John Cauldwell, James Hughes, Hugh M'Kenna, Robert M'Kenna and Henry Sexton). Joseph M'Kenna had announced that he did not seek any vote, but his name was not withdrawn in time. Of the 1,100 electors only 467 voted. M'Garvey (chairman of the council) and M'Kee were seeking re-election."
